# infrastructure.rules
version: 1

## MUST
- No hardcoded secrets, access keys, or credentials in Terraform/IaC files, CI config, or scripts.
- Every resource that can be destroyed or replaced by a change is reviewed for `prevent_destroy`/lifecycle implications before merge.
- IaC changes must pass `validate`/`plan` (or equivalent) with no errors.

## SHOULD
- Destructive-looking plan diffs (resource replacement, deletion) are called out explicitly in the PR description.
- New infrastructure includes tagging/labeling consistent with existing conventions.

## SECURITY
- No security group / firewall / ingress rule opens a port to `0.0.0.0/0` (or equivalent) without a one-line justification.
- IAM/role policies follow least privilege; no new wildcard-action or wildcard-resource grants without justification.
- State files and secrets backends are never committed to the repo.

## ARCHITECTURE
- Changes to shared/base modules used by multiple environments are called out as such in the PR description.
